unched my wall a few times uh  whether it was  yeah whether it was from like complete  stricken fear  or me like shooting around the corner uh  at one combine  pulling a grenade out of the air and  tossing it in the other direction and  just i'm  smashing my fist with all those marks on  my wall uh because of that  that was a fault of me be like trying to  be like i want to do the standing up i  want to be full force this is my first  vr experience because otherwise all my  vr experiences leading up to this  um have been like smaller games and a  lot of them  are honestly made me sick or i found  really gimmicky  and not and i was kind of skeptical of  the entire medium at this point being  like  i'll just have to wait and see where  this goes years from now  but after playing this game my  skepticism is gone  like i like it's like i'm all i'm  so unbelievably all into the point where  like i've said this many times but i  think it like i think it's ruined me  one flat  there's one last thing that we need to  talk about so we're not gonna spoil  anything for any of those who are  watching this who hasn't played it but  it's important that we do talk about  the final act of this game which we've  talked a lot about what it's done for  the  medium we've talked a lot about what  half-life has done just  for games in general but this ending the  ending of this game  kind of does a little more uh that it's  it's hard to explain but i but it  recontextualizes  the entire franchise i think it  completely repositions everything we've  we've played it we've played and seen in  these games and puts it in a different  light so jake you are enough  you were not familiar with half-life  prior this or at least you were like not  someone like maybe like michael and i  who love the franchise  tell me about that experience because i  have my own kind of reaction to that  whole thing but i really want to hear  from you and like how that kind of  meshed and molded your entire experien